## 1. Los Angeles (≈ 5 km from the hotel)

| Attraction | Type | Highlights | Opening Hours | Ticket Price (adults) |
|------------|------|------------|---------------|-----------------------|
| **Universal Studios Hollywood** | Theme park | Studio tour, 4D rides, The Wizarding World of Harry Potter | 9 am–9 pm | $109 |
| **Griffith Observatory** | Observatory | Panoramic city views, free public telescopes | 10 am–6 pm | Free |
| **The Getty Center** | Museum | Art collections, gardens, architecture | 10 am–5 pm | Free |
| **Hollywood Walk of Fame** | Outdoor | Stars, TCL Chinese Theatre, Dolby Theatre | 24 h | Free |
| **LACMA (Los Angeles County Museum of Art)** | Museum | Contemporary art, Urban Light installation | 10 am–5 pm | $25 |

> **Why it’s fun** – LA is a sprawling playground of culture, cinema, and theme‑park thrills. The Hollywood Walk of Fame is a must‑see for a quick photo‑op, while Universal Studios offers a full day of rides and behind‑the‑scenes fun.

---

## 2. Santa Monica (≈ 12 km from the hotel)

| Attraction | Type | Highlights | Opening Hours | Ticket Price (adults) |
|------------|------|------------|---------------|-----------------------|
| **Santa Monica Pier & Aquarium** | Pier / Aquarium | Classic pier rides, sea‑life exhibits | 10 am–6 pm | $15 |
| **Third Street Promenade** | Shopping / Street fair | Boutiques, street performers, food trucks | 10 am–9 pm | Free |
| **Santa Monica Beach** | Beach | Surfing, volleyball, sunset views | 24 h | Free |
| **Annenberg Community Beach House** | Community center | Pools, art exhibits, kids’ programs | 10 am–6 pm | $10 |
| **Santa Monica Farmers Market** | Market | Fresh produce, local crafts | 9 am–2 pm | Free |

> **Why it’s fun** – Santa Monica blends classic beach vibes with a lively downtown scene. The pier is great for a quick ride on the carousel, while the Promenade offers a relaxed stroll with plenty of food and entertainment.

---

## 3. Beverly Hills (≈ 8 km from the hotel)

| Attraction | Type | Highlights | Opening Hours | Ticket Price (adults) |
|------------|------|------------|---------------|-----------------------|
| **Rodeo Drive** | Shopping | Luxury boutiques, celebrity sightings | 10 am–8 pm | Free |
| **Beverly Hills Hotel** | Historic hotel | Iconic architecture, rooftop bar | 24 h | Free (bar only) |
| **Beverly Hills Farmers Market** | Market | Organic produce, artisanal goods | 9 am–2 pm | Free |
| **The Beverly Hills Hotel’s “The Rooftop”** | Rooftop bar | Sunset cocktails, panoramic city views | 5 pm–11 pm | $25 |
| **Beverly Hills Park** | Park | Dog park, walking trails | 6 am–10 pm | Free |

> **Why it’s fun** – Beverly Hills is all about luxury and glamour. Even if you’re not splurging, a walk down Rodeo Drive is a visual treat, and the rooftop bar offers a great spot to watch the sunset over the city.

